# tsup output. v1.1.0 dropped the committed dist/ — package.json#main points at
# the flat ./react.js and consumers install from a git tag.
# dist/ is COMMITTED (v1.2). Every consumer installs from a git tag, and a git
# install runs no lifecycle script — a dist built only at publish time exists for
# nobody. `npm run check:build` fails if it is stale.
# dist/
# Both halves. Comparison is a byte-exact PNG match, so a baseline is valid only
# on the machine that recorded it — committing this box's set would make CI
# permanently red rather than green. CI must record its own inside its image.
